cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MINDIR, please cite it as below. (DOI to be assigned on release; do not cite a fabricated DOI.)"
title: "MINDIR: subject-specific geometry and calibration of internal visual states"
version: "0.1.0-rc1"
date-released: "2026-09-26"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "TBD"
    family-names: "TBD"
    affiliation: "TBD (MSc Cognitive Science)"
keywords:
  - fMRI
  - mental imagery
  - representational geometry
  - reproducibility
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/toniIepure25/FMRI2images"
abstract: >
  MINDIR is a research platform for studying perception-to-imagery neural representational geometry, minimal
  target-state calibration, and its acquisition robustness. Findings to date are from a closed development
  cohort; an independent replication is preregistered and frozen but not yet executed. No biological
  generalization is claimed.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "A massive 7T fMRI dataset (Natural Scenes Dataset)"
    authors: [{family-names: "Allen", given-names: "E. J."}]
    year: 2022
    notes: "Dataset used by the development cohort; DOI to be confirmed by authors."
